ker (18-24) in Dehradun, dedicated to his craft and eager for his bakery products to stand out, especially during festive seasons.\n• beforeProblem: He struggles toyhgfgh find packaging or product designs that genuinely convey luxury and elegance, causing his artisanal bakery items to blend in with competitors and miss opportunities to attract customers seeking premium looks for special occasions.\n• beforeEmotion: Disappointed, frustrated, uninspired, feeling his hard work and product quality are not fully reflected by the presentation.\n• beforeEnvironment: A typical, moderately lit bakery counter or a cluttered retail shelf, where products with generic, unappealing packaging sit unnoticed.\n• beforeText: Product B: \'Ordinary, uninspired packaging that fails to capture attention. Your craftsmanship deserves better presentation, especially for festive joy.\'\n• afterSupport: Product Prerna provides a sophisticated and high-quality design solution with luxurious packaging, enabling his bakery items to project a premium image that captivates customers and perfectly aligns with festive buying motivations.\n• afterOutcome: His products gain significant attention and admiration, particularly during festivals, leading to increased sales, an enhanced brand reputation, and loyal customers who consistently appreciate the luxurious and thoughtful presentation.\n• afterEmotion: Confident, proud, successful, elevated, delighted by increased customer engagement and appreciation.\n• afterText: Product Prerna: \'Luxurious, captivating design that commands attention and boosts festive sales. Elevate your brand with unparalleled elegance!\'\n• mood: Transformative, aspirational, elegant, empowering, contrasting success.\n• theme: The power of superior presentation; transforming everyday products into luxury experiences; achieving business success through refined design.\n• tone: Inspiring, sophisticated, persuasive, confident, premium, discerning.\n• colorPreference: For \'before\', muted and uninspiring tones like dull greys, basic whites, or standard browns. For \'after\', rich and opulent colors such as deep gold, regal navy blue, emerald green, or luxurious maroon, often complemented with elegant silver or bronze accents, evoking festivity and high-end appeal.\n• finishType: High-resolution, polished, and refined product photography with sharp details and a sense of premium texture for \'after\'. For \'before\', a slightly duller, less vibrant, or more utilitarian finish to highlight the stark contrast. Clean, modern, and aesthetically pleasing composition.',1,'2026-03-09 05:20:16',0,NULL),(9,60,'visuals | comparative | Product A vs Product B','==============================\n      VISUAL INFORMATION\n      ==============================\n\n      Mode: visuals\n      Media Type: comparative\n      Media Sub Type: Product A vs Product B\n\n\n      ------------------------------\n      BUSINESS INFORMATION\n      ------------------------------\n      • Business Id: 1\n• Profile Id: 1\n• Business Name: visualgrab\n• Created At: 2026-02-09T20:11:56\n• Updated At: 2026-03-06T16:14:06\n• Is Completed: 1\n• Business Type: Advertising & Marketing\n• Industry: Advertising Agency\n• Year Established: 2010\n• Terms Accepted: 1\n• Privacy Accepted: 1\n\n      ------------------------------\n      PERSONA INFORMATION\n      ------------------------------\n      \n          Persona Name: persona1\n\n          • demographic - Age: 18–24\n• demographic - Gender: Male\n• demographic - Income: 1-2 lakh between\n• demographic - Education: 12th pass\n• demographic - Occupation: bakery\n• geographic - Country: Canada\n• geographic - Climate: Cool\n• geographic - Buying Motivation: Luxury Looks in Packaging\n• geographic - State / City: Dehradun, Uttrakhand\n• geographic - Urban or Rural: Urban\n• behavioural - Buying Behaviour: as per the season and festival\n• behavioural - Usage Rate: 100\n• behavioural - Brand Loyalty: Honesty\n          \n\n      -------